        "thinking": "I'm identifying the form अक्लदिषि as लुङ् कर्तरि उत्तमपुरुष एकवचन from root क्लदि, which the Dhatupatha lists under भ्वादि as \"क्लदि आह्वाने रोदने च\" meaning to call out or weep, and checking whether it's परस्मैपदी.\n\nSince इदित् roots take नुम् agama, an इदित् क्लदि would give अक्लन्दिषि, but the given form अक्लदिषि lacks the nasal, so the root must be non-इदित्. I also consider क्लिदू (दिवादि, meaning to become moist), but that would yield अक्लेदिषि instead, so that's not matching either.\n\nSince it's ātmanepadi, लङ् उत्तम एकवचन आत्मनेपद gives अक्लदे as the answer.\n\n",
